            <ArticleTitle>Ectopic Pancreas in the Wall of the Small Intestine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1407-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11605-016-3104-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ectopic pancreas is an uncommon and benign finding. However, these lesions can cause symptoms including abdominal pain and often require removal. We present the case of a 27-year-old patient with long-standing vague abdominal symptoms eventually found to have ectopic pancreas tissue in the proximal jejunum.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
